## 26 U.S.C. § 36B(c)(1) Applicable taxpayer

"(A) In general. The term "applicable taxpayer" means, with respect to any
taxable year, a taxpayer whose household income for the taxable year equals
or exceeds 100 percent but does not exceed 400 percent of an amount equal to
the poverty line for a family of the size involved. (B) Special rule for
certain individuals lawfully present in the United States. If (i) a taxpayer
has a household income which is not greater than 100 percent of an amount
equal to the poverty line for a family of the size involved, and (ii) the
taxpayer is an alien lawfully present in the United States, but is not
eligible for the medicaid program under title XIX of the Social Security Act
by reason of such alien status, the taxpayer shall, for purposes of the credit
under this section, be treated as an applicable taxpayer [...]. (C) Married
couples must file joint return. If the taxpayer is married (within the meaning
of section 7703) at the close of the taxable year, the taxpayer shall be
treated as an applicable taxpayer only if the taxpayer and the taxpayer's
spouse file a joint return for the taxable year. (D) Denial of credit to
dependents. No credit shall be allowed under this section to any individual
with respect to whom a deduction under section 151 is allowable to another
taxpayer [...]. (E) Temporary rule for 2021 through 2025. In the case of a
taxable year beginning after December 31, 2020, and before January 1, 2026,
subparagraph (A) shall be applied without regard to "but does not exceed 400
percent"."

26 CFR 1.36B-2(b)(2)(ii): "a married taxpayer satisfies the joint filing
requirement [...] if the taxpayer files a tax return using a filing status of
married filing separately and the taxpayer (A) Is living apart from the
taxpayer's spouse at the time the taxpayer files the tax return; (B) Is unable
to file a joint return because the taxpayer is a victim of domestic abuse
[...] or spousal abandonment [...]". (v) "Three-year rule. Paragraph
(b)(2)(ii) of this section does not apply if the taxpayer met the
requirements of paragraph (b)(2)(ii) of this section for each of the three
preceding taxable years." 1.36B-2(b)(6) treats a taxpayer below 100 percent
as an applicable taxpayer when "(C) Advance credit payments are authorized and
paid for one or more months during the taxable year" (and the Exchange
estimated an income of 100 to 400 percent).

DF asks these as yes/no questions: the MFS exception (Exception 2,
`i8962--2024.pdf` p 6 to 7) and its fourth straight year; for a taxpayer
below 100 percent with no APTC, whether someone on the plan is not eligible
for Medicaid because of immigration status (36B(c)(1)(B)); the dependent
taxpayer questions (36B(c)(1)(D)). A married head of household whose spouse
is not residency-eligible for a joint return and who did not live apart from
the spouse for the last six months is treated as married (36B(c)(1)(C)). A
fact DF leaves Incomplete here counts as "applicable", as in DF
(`/potentiallyApplicableTaxPayer` is true when `/notPtcApplicableTaxPayer` is
Incomplete).

```catala
scope PtcAllowed:
  # DF: /maybeEligibleForPtc
  definition maybe_eligible_for_ptc equals
    not (filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
         and is_mfj_dependent)

  # DF: /dependentTpOtherMembersArePartOfDifferentTaxFamily (asked only if
  # the dependent taxpayer enrolled someone else)
  definition dependent_tp_other_members_are_part_of_different_tax_family equals
    dependent_tp_enrolled_someone_else
    and writable_dependent_tp_other_members_are_part_of_different_tax_family

  # DF: /dependentTpNeedToCollectMoreInfo
  definition dependent_tp_need_to_collect_more_info equals
    ((not primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent)
     and dependent_tp_self_enrolled and (not dependent_tp_enrolled_someone_else))
    or ((not dependent_tp_self_enrolled) and dependent_tp_enrolled_someone_else
        and (not dependent_tp_other_members_are_part_of_different_tax_family))
    or ((not primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent)
        and dependent_tp_self_enrolled and dependent_tp_enrolled_someone_else
        and (not dependent_tp_other_members_are_part_of_different_tax_family))

  # DF: /hasPtcQualifyingPlan. Incomplete in DF when not maybe eligible,
  # which DF reads as "no Form 8962"; false here.
  rule has_ptc_qualifying_plan under condition
    maybe_eligible_for_ptc
    and (if not_mfj_and_primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits
         then dependent_tp_need_to_collect_more_info
         else writable_has_ptc_qualifying_plan)
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /hasAdvancedPtc (asked only with a qualifying plan)
  rule has_advanced_ptc under condition
    has_ptc_qualifying_plan and writable_has_advanced_ptc
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 36B(c)(1)(C), 26 CFR 1.36B-2(b)(2). DF: /isMFSAndCantBeClaimed
  rule is_mfs_and_cant_be_claimed under condition
    filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
    and not not_mfj_and_primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits
  consequence fulfilled

  # 26 CFR 1.36B-2(b)(2)(ii). DF: /hasMfsException
  rule has_mfs_exception under condition
    is_mfs_and_cant_be_claimed and writable_has_mfs_exception
  consequence fulfilled

  # 26 CFR 1.36B-2(b)(2)(v). DF: /claimingMfsExceptionForFourthStraightYear
  rule claiming_mfs_exception_for_fourth_straight_year under condition
    has_mfs_exception and writable_claiming_mfs_exception_for_fourth_straight_year
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 36B(c)(1)(C) and (D). DF: /notPtcApplicableTaxPayerSoFar
  rule not_ptc_applicable_tax_payer_so_far under condition
    (is_mfs_and_cant_be_claimed
     and ((not has_mfs_exception)
          or claiming_mfs_exception_for_fourth_straight_year))
    or not_mfj_and_primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 36B(c)(1)(A), Form 8962 line 5 below 100.
  # DF: /isBelow100PercentFederalPovertyLevel
  rule is_below100_percent_federal_poverty_level under condition
    household_income_as_percent < P.ptc_applicable_taxpayer_poverty_percent_floor
  consequence fulfilled

  # 26 CFR 1.36B-2(b)(6)(i)(C): with APTC paid, a household income below 100
  # percent does not disqualify. DF:
  # /maybeApplicableTpAndNoAptcAndBelow100PovertyThreshold
  rule maybe_applicable_tp_and_no_aptc_and_below100_poverty_threshold under condition
    (not not_ptc_applicable_tax_payer_so_far) and (not has_advanced_ptc)
    and is_below100_percent_federal_poverty_level
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 36B(c)(1)(C) (married head of household treated as married) and
  # (D) (dependent taxpayer with no APTC who enrolled self or own family).
  # DF: /filerNotQualifiedForPtcBecauseOfStatusAndResidenceInfo. Its first
  # branch asks IsComplete(/hasAdvancedPtc), which is
  # /hasPtcQualifyingPlan.
  rule filer_not_qualified_for_ptc_because_of_status_and_residence_info under condition
    (has_ptc_qualifying_plan
     and filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
     and is_married
     and (not secondary_filer_residency_eligible_for_mfj)
     and (not lived_apart_last_six_months))
    or ((not has_advanced_ptc)
        and not_mfj_and_primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits
        and (not primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent)
        and (dependent_tp_self_enrolled
             or (dependent_tp_enrolled_someone_else
                 and not dependent_tp_other_members_are_part_of_different_tax_family)))
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 36B(c)(1). DF: /notPtcApplicableTaxPayer, where
  # /below100ThresholdAndNotEligibleForMedicaidBecauseOfImmigrationStatus is
  # the writable answer when asked (36B(c)(1)(B)) and Incomplete otherwise.
  rule not_ptc_applicable_tax_payer under condition
    not_ptc_applicable_tax_payer_so_far
    or (maybe_applicable_tp_and_no_aptc_and_below100_poverty_threshold
        and not writable_below100_threshold_and_not_eligible_for_medicaid_because_of_immigration_status)
    or filer_not_qualified_for_ptc_because_of_status_and_residence_info
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /potentiallyApplicableTaxPayer (/uniqueCircumstancesIsComplete is a
  # UI completeness flag, true for complete inputs)
  rule potentially_applicable_tax_payer under condition
    not not_ptc_applicable_tax_payer
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /applicableTaxPayerOrHasAptc
  rule applicable_tax_payer_or_has_aptc under condition
    potentially_applicable_tax_payer or has_advanced_ptc
  consequence fulfilled
```

## 26 U.S.C. § 36B(c)(2) Coverage month, per Form 1095-A

"(A) In general. The term "coverage month" means, with respect to an
applicable taxpayer, any month if (i) as of the first day of such month the
taxpayer, the taxpayer's spouse, or any dependent of the taxpayer is covered
by a qualified health plan [...] that was enrolled in through an Exchange
[...], and (ii) the premium for coverage under such plan for such month is
paid by the taxpayer (or through advance payment of the credit [...]). (B)
Exception for minimum essential coverage. (i) In general. The term "coverage
month" shall not include any month with respect to an individual if for such
month the individual is eligible for minimum essential coverage other than
[...] coverage in the individual market."

26 CFR 1.36B-3(c)(2): "Certain individuals enrolled during a month. If an
individual enrolls in a qualified health plan and the enrollment is effective
on the date of the individual's birth, adoption, or placement for adoption or
in foster care, or on the effective date of a court order, the individual is
treated as enrolled as of the first day of that month".

DF offers as possible coverage months the months covered on their first day
(`/1095As/*/monthOptions`): the starting month if the policy starts on the 1st
or the policy-date exception (1.36B-3(c)(2)) applies, and every later month up
to the end month. The taxpayer then picks the coverage months among them
(`coverageMonths`), which carries the premium-paid and minimum-essential-coverage
tests of 36B(c)(2)(A)(ii) and (B). DF reads policy dates only for a
potentially applicable taxpayer (`/1095As/*/policyStartDate`), so with no
applicable taxpayer no month is active or a coverage month. The policy dates
are 2024 dates and the end is not before the start (DF
`/1095As/*/hasPolicyDateError`).

DF-BUG(31): DF's December option (`ptc.xml` lines 3549 to 3574) is "the
policy does not start in December and ends in December, or starts in
December with the policy-date exception". It omits "starts on December 1",
which every other month has, so a policy starting on December 1 never has
December as a coverage month although the taxpayer is covered on December 1.
The statute rule is used: the starting month counts when the policy starts on
the 1st, December included.

Form 1095-A amounts by month (DF `/1095As/*/ptcMonthlyPremium<Month>`,
`ptcMonthlySlcspPremium<Month>`, `ptcMonthlyAptcPremium<Month>`): when DF
asked the annual line 33 amount instead of the months (a full-year policy
with no change), the month is one twelfth of it. The enrollment premium
(column A) and the APTC (column C) count in every month the policy is active;
the SLCSP premium (column B) only in coverage months.

DF-BUG(32), first part: DF uses the annual SLCSP divided by 12 in every
month, coverage month or not (`/1095As/*/ptcMonthlySlcspPremiumJan`, line
5006). Only coverage months have a premium assistance amount
(IRC 36B(b)(1)), so a non-coverage month has an SLCSP of $0 here. In DF this
matters only when such a form reaches the monthly path (see the second part
below).

```catala
scope Form1095ACalculation:
  definition start_month equals Date.get_month of form.writable_policy_start_date
  definition start_day equals Date.get_day of form.writable_policy_start_date
  definition end_month equals Date.get_month of form.writable_policy_end_date

  # 26 CFR 1.36B-3(c)(2). DF: /1095As/*/hasPolicyDateException and
  # /1095As/*/maybeHasPolicyDateException
  rule has_policy_date_exception under condition
    potentially_applicable_tax_payer
    and form.writable_special_policy_modification_in_starting_month
    and start_day != 1
    and form.writable_has_policy_date_exception
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /1095As/*/eligibleForCoverageMonths
  rule eligible_for_coverage_months under condition
    form.has_coverage_months and potentially_applicable_tax_payer
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /1095As/*/hasPolicyForAllMonths (starts in January, ends in December)
  rule has_policy_for_all_months under condition
    potentially_applicable_tax_payer and start_month = 1 and end_month = 12
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 36B(c)(2)(A)(i): covered as of the first day of the month
  # (DF: /1095As/*/monthOptions), chosen by the taxpayer and eligible
  # (DF: /1095As/*/has<Month>CoverageMonth).
  # DF-BUG(31): the "starts on the 1st" case applies to December too.
  definition coverage_month_numbers equals
    list of m among (List.sequence of 1, 13) such that
      ((start_month = m
        and (start_day = 1 or has_policy_date_exception))
       or (start_month < m and m <= end_month))
      and (form.coverage_months contains m)
      and eligible_for_coverage_months

  definition months equals
    map each m among (List.sequence of 1, 13) to
      (let policy_is_active equals
         potentially_applicable_tax_payer
         and start_month <= m and m <= end_month
       in
       let is_coverage_month equals coverage_month_numbers contains m in
       Form1095AMonth {
         -- month_number: m
         -- policy_is_active: policy_is_active
         -- is_coverage_month: is_coverage_month
         -- premium:
              if not policy_is_active then $0
              else if ptc_annual_premium_is_known
              then form.writable_ptc_annual_premium * (1.0 / 12.0)
              else month_amount of form.writable_ptc_monthly_premium, m
         # DF-BUG(32): $0 outside coverage months
         -- slcsp_premium:
              if not is_coverage_month then $0
              else if no_changes_and12_month_policy
              then form.writable_slcsp_annual_premium * (1.0 / 12.0)
              else month_amount of form.writable_ptc_monthly_slcsp_premium, m
         -- aptc:
              if aptc_annual_amount_is_known
              then aptc_annual_amount * (1.0 / 12.0)
              else if has_advanced_ptc and policy_is_active
              then month_amount of form.writable_ptc_monthly_aptc_premium, m
              else $0
       })

  # DF: /1095As/*/numberOfCoverageMonths
  definition number_of_coverage_months equals
    number of coverage_month_numbers

  rule has_zero_coverage_months under condition
    number_of_coverage_months = 0
  consequence fulfilled

  rule has_at_least_one_coverage_month under condition
    number_of_coverage_months >= 1
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /1095As/*/premiumsOrSlcspChange is a Switch on these two facts
  rule premiums_or_slcsp_change_is_asked under condition
    has_at_least_one_coverage_month and has_policy_for_all_months
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /1095As/*/ptcAnnualPremium
  rule ptc_annual_premium_is_known under condition
    premiums_or_slcsp_change_is_asked
    and not form.writable_premiums_or_slcsp_change
  consequence fulfilled

  # Form 8962 line 10, i8962 p 12: "You were enrolled in the qualified health
  # plan for all 12 months during 2024. Your enrollment premium was the same
  # for every month [...] Your SLCSP premium is the same for every month".
  # DF: /1095As/*/noChangesAnd12MonthPolicy
  rule no_changes_and12_month_policy under condition
    premiums_or_slcsp_change_is_asked
    and (not form.writable_premiums_or_slcsp_change)
    and (not form.has_change_in_circumstance)
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /1095As/*/aptcAnnualAmount (DF asks line 33 column C for a
  # full-year policy with no change or a form with no coverage month)
  rule aptc_annual_amount_is_known under condition
    no_changes_and12_month_policy or has_zero_coverage_months
  consequence fulfilled

  definition aptc_annual_amount equals
    if has_advanced_ptc and aptc_annual_amount_is_known
    then form.writable_aptc_annual_amount
    else $0

  # DF: /1095As/*/hasCoverageMonthsOrAptc
  rule has_coverage_months_or_aptc under condition
    has_at_least_one_coverage_month or has_advanced_ptc
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF-BUG(32): second part. Form 8962 line 10 (i8962 p 12): annual totals
  # only if "You were enrolled in the qualified health plan for all 12 months
  # during 2024", with the same premium and SLCSP every month. DF's filter is
  # /noChangesAnd12MonthPolicy, which tests only that the policy starts in
  # January and ends in December: a policy starting on January 20 without
  # the policy-date exception (11 coverage months), or a taxpayer who
  # deselected a month (minimum essential coverage, unpaid premium), still
  # gets line 11, which allows the full-year SLCSP for a month that is not a
  # coverage month (IRC 36B(b)(1)). Here line 11 needs 12 coverage months;
  # otherwise the monthly path uses the twelfths in the coverage months only.
  # The second branch is DF's: no coverage month but APTC paid, so line 11(f)
  # reports the APTC to repay (i8962 p 14, "Not an applicable taxpayer").
  rule can_report_annual_totals under condition
    (no_changes_and12_month_policy and number_of_coverage_months = 12)
    or (has_zero_coverage_months and has_advanced_ptc)
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /1095As/*/ptcAnnualPremium, as summed by /totalPtcAnnualPremium
  definition annual_premium equals
    if ptc_annual_premium_is_known then form.writable_ptc_annual_premium
    else $0

  # DF: /1095As/*/slcspAnnualPremium, as summed by /totalAnnualSlcspPremium
  definition annual_slcsp_premium equals
    if no_changes_and12_month_policy then form.writable_slcsp_annual_premium
    else $0
```

## The Forms 1095-A of the return

```catala
scope PtcAllowed:
  definition forms equals
    map each f among form1095_as to
      (output of Form1095ACalculation with {
         -- form: f
         -- potentially_applicable_tax_payer: potentially_applicable_tax_payer
         -- has_advanced_ptc: has_advanced_ptc
       })

  definition all_months equals
    combine all c among forms in acc initially [] with acc ++ c.months

  # DF: /mayNeedToFileForm8962
  rule may_need_to_file_form8962 under condition
    (exists c among forms such that c.has_coverage_months_or_aptc)
    and maybe_eligible_for_ptc and has_ptc_qualifying_plan
    and applicable_tax_payer_or_has_aptc
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /needsToFileForm8962
  rule needs_to_file_form8962 under condition may_need_to_file_form8962
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /ptcHasZeroCoverageMonths (Incomplete in DF, false here, when there
  # is no form or no applicable taxpayer and no APTC)
  rule ptc_has_zero_coverage_months under condition
    applicable_tax_payer_or_has_aptc
    and number of forms > 0
    and (for all c among forms we have c.has_zero_coverage_months)
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /qualifiedForPtc
  rule qualified_for_ptc under condition
    has_ptc_qualifying_plan
    and (not filer_not_qualified_for_ptc_because_of_status_and_residence_info)
    and potentially_applicable_tax_payer
    and number of forms > 0
    and not ptc_has_zero_coverage_months
  consequence fulfilled
```

## Form 8962 line 11: annual totals

Line 10 (`i8962--2024.pdf` p 12): "Check "Yes" and continue to line 11 if
all of the following apply for each qualified health plan you or a member of
your tax family was enrolled in for 2024. Otherwise, check "No" and continue
to lines 12 through 23."

Line 11 (p 13 to 14): "Column (a). Enter the annual enrollment premiums from
Form 1095-A, line 33, column A. If you have more than one Form 1095-A, add the
amounts together [...]. Column (b). Enter the annual applicable SLCSP premium
from Form 1095-A, line 33, column B. [...] Column (c). Enter the amount from
line 8a of Form 8962. Column (d). Subtract the amount in column (c) from the
amount in column (b). If the result is zero or less, enter -0-. Column (e).
Enter the lesser of the amount in column (a) or the amount in column (d).
[...] Column (f). Enter the APTC amount from Form 1095-A, line 33, column C.
If you have more than one Form 1095-A, add the amounts together".

DF-BUG(33): DF's `/ptcCanReportAnnualTotals` (line 6456) is true if *any*
Form 1095-A allows annual totals; the instruction says "for each qualified
health plan". DF's own comment marks it as a TODO. Every form is required
here. It matters only with two or more forms, which DF blocks
(`ko_tp_needs_to_delete1095_a`).

DF rounds each column total to whole dollars (`Round` of the
`CollectionSum`).

```catala
scope PtcAllowed:
  # DF-BUG(33): every form, not any form.
  rule ptc_can_report_annual_totals under condition
    number of forms > 0
    and (for all c among forms we have c.can_report_annual_totals)
  consequence fulfilled

  # Line 11(a). DF: /totalPtcAnnualPremium
  definition total_ptc_annual_premium equals
    round of (Money.sum of (map each c among forms to c.annual_premium))

  # Line 11(b). DF: /totalAnnualSlcspPremium. With several forms the
  # instruction enters one form's SLCSP per state; several forms are
  # knocked out (ko_tp_needs_to_delete1095_a), and DF adds them.
  definition total_annual_slcsp_premium equals
    round of (Money.sum of (map each c among forms to c.annual_slcsp_premium))

  # Line 11(f). DF: /totalAnnualAptcAmount
  definition total_annual_aptc_amount equals
    round of (Money.sum of (map each c among forms to c.aptc_annual_amount))

  # Line 11(d), IRC 36B(b)(2)(B). DF: /annualMaxPremiumAssitance
  definition annual_max_premium_assistance equals
    Money.positive of (total_annual_slcsp_premium - ptc_annual_contribution_amount)

  # Line 11(e), IRC 36B(b)(2). DF: /annualPtcAllowed
  definition annual_ptc_allowed equals
    Money.min of annual_max_premium_assistance, total_ptc_annual_premium
```

## Form 8962 lines 12 to 23: monthly calculation

26 U.S.C. § 36B(b)(1): "The term "premium assistance credit amount" means,
with respect to any taxable year, the sum of the premium assistance amounts
determined under paragraph (2) with respect to all coverage months of the
taxpayer occurring during the taxable year. (2) Premium assistance amount. The
premium assistance amount determined under this subsection with respect to
any coverage month is the amount equal to the lesser of (A) the monthly
premiums for such month for 1 or more qualified health plans [...], or (B)
the excess (if any) of (i) the adjusted monthly premium for such month for the
applicable second lowest cost silver plan with respect to the taxpayer, over
(ii) an amount equal to 1/12 of the product of the applicable percentage and
the taxpayer's household income for the taxable year."

Lines 12 to 23 (`i8962--2024.pdf` p 14 to 15): "Column (a). Enter [...] the
amount of the monthly premiums reported on Form 1095-A, lines 21 through 32,
column A, for the corresponding month. If you have more than one Form 1095-A
affecting a particular month, add the amounts together for that month [...].
Column (c). [...] enter on lines 12 through 23, column (c), your monthly
contribution amount from line 8b. If columns (a) and (b) of any of lines 12
through 23 are blank, leave column (c) of the corresponding line blank. [...]
Column (d). Subtract the amount in column (c) from the amount in column (b).
If the result is zero or less, enter -0-. Column (e). Enter for each month the
lesser of the amount in column (a) or the amount in column (d) for that month.
[...] Column (f). Enter on lines 12 through 23, column (f), the amount of the
monthly APTC reported on Form 1095-A, lines 21 through 32, column C. If you
have more than one Form 1095-A affecting a particular month, add the amounts
together".

DF fills a month only when some policy is active that month
(`/hasActive1095APolicyIn<Month>`) and otherwise leaves it Incomplete, which
its totals count as $0; here such a month is all $0. DF rounds each month's
column sum to whole dollars.

```catala
scope PtcAllowed:
  # DF: /needsToFileForm8962Monthly
  rule needs_to_file_form8962_monthly under condition
    may_need_to_file_form8962 and not ptc_can_report_annual_totals
  consequence fulfilled

  definition ptc_months equals
    map each m among (List.sequence of 1, 13) to
      (let rows equals list of r among all_months such that r.month_number = m in
       let has_active_policy equals
         exists r among rows such that r.policy_is_active
       in
       let filled equals needs_to_file_form8962_monthly and has_active_policy in
       # (a) DF: /monthlyPtcPremiumFor<Month>
       let enrollment_premium equals
         if filled then round of (Money.sum of (map each r among rows to r.premium))
         else $0
       in
       # (b) DF: /monthlyPtcSlcspPremiumFor<Month>
       let slcsp_premium equals
         if filled
         then round of (Money.sum of (map each r among rows to r.slcsp_premium))
         else $0
       in
       # (c) DF: /monthlyPtcContributionAmountFor<Month>
       let contribution_amount equals
         if filled then ptc_monthly_contribution_amount else $0
       in
       # (d) IRC 36B(b)(2)(B). DF: /monthlyPtcMaxPremiumAssitanceFor<Month>
       let max_premium_assistance equals
         Money.positive of (slcsp_premium - contribution_amount)
       in
       PtcMonth {
         -- month_number: m
         -- has_active_policy: has_active_policy
         -- enrollment_premium: enrollment_premium
         -- slcsp_premium: slcsp_premium
         -- contribution_amount: contribution_amount
         -- max_premium_assistance: max_premium_assistance
         # (e) IRC 36B(b)(2). DF: /monthlyPtcAllowedFor<Month>
         -- ptc_allowed: Money.min of max_premium_assistance, enrollment_premium
         # (f) DF: /monthlyAptcPremiumFor<Month>
         -- advance_payment:
              if filled then round of (Money.sum of (map each r among rows to r.aptc))
              else $0
       })
```

## Form 8962 lines 24 and 25

"Line 24. Enter the amount from line 11(e) or add lines 12(e) through 23(e)
and enter the total. Line 25. Enter the amount from line 11(f) or add lines
12(f) through 23(f) and enter the total." (`i8962--2024.pdf` p 15.)

With no Form 8962 (`needs_to_file_form8962` false) both lines are $0; DF
leaves them Incomplete on the monthly side and computes the annual side
anyway, but reads neither without a Form 8962.

```catala
scope PtcAllowed:
  # Line 24, IRC 36B(b)(1). DF: /totalPtcAmountAllowed
  definition total_ptc_amount_allowed equals
    if not may_need_to_file_form8962 then $0
    else if ptc_can_report_annual_totals then annual_ptc_allowed
    else Money.sum of (map each r among ptc_months to r.ptc_allowed)

  # Line 25, IRC 36B(f). DF: /totalAptcAmountTaken
  definition total_aptc_amount_taken equals
    if not may_need_to_file_form8962 then $0
    else if ptc_can_report_annual_totals then total_annual_aptc_amount
    else Money.sum of (map each r among ptc_months to r.advance_payment)

  # DF: /netPtcAmount (part 3 owns line 26)
  definition net_ptc_amount equals
    total_ptc_amount_allowed - total_aptc_amount_taken
```

## Knockouts and blocked submissions

`flow.xml` lines 96 to 103 knock out a return when any of the following is
true; the two `BlockSubmissionOnTrue` facts of `ptc.xml` (lines 1027 and
1042) stop the filing too, and are knockouts here (CONVENTIONS section 6).
Each is a case the module does not compute:

- allocation of policy amounts with another taxpayer (Form 8962 line 9 and
  Part IV, `i8962--2024.pdf` p 10 to 12): `ko_dependent_tp_requires_allocations`,
  `ko_needs_allocations`;
- a qualified small employer health reimbursement arrangement (line 11(e)
  and 12(e) "Note. Do not follow this instruction if you were provided a
  QSEHRA", p 14): `ko_has_ptc_qualifying_plan_and_qsehra`;
- an offer of employer coverage (IRC 36B(c)(2)(C), affordability and minimum
  value): `ko_has_employer_sponsored_plan`;
- a dependent required to file, whose modified AGI joins the household income
  (IRC 36B(d)(2)(A)(ii), Form 8962 line 2b): `ko_dependents_required_to_file`;
- more than one Form 1095-A (several SLCSP rules, line 11(b) p 13 to 14):
  `ko_self_reported_has_multiple1095_as`, `ko_tp_needs_to_delete1095_a`;
- immigration-status rules (Pub. 974, "Individuals Not Lawfully Present"):
  `ko_has_immigration_status_not_eligible_for_marketplace`;
- the alternative calculation for year of marriage (line 9 and Part V):
  `ko_wants_to_use_alt_calculations`;
- a qualifying plan reported with no Form 1095-A: `ko_tp_needs_to_add1095_a`.

```catala
scope PtcAllowed:
  # DF: /dependentTpRequiresAllocations
  rule ko_dependent_tp_requires_allocations under condition
    not_mfj_and_primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits
    and dependent_tp_self_enrolled and dependent_tp_enrolled_someone_else
    and ((primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent
          and not dependent_tp_other_members_are_part_of_different_tax_family)
         or ((not primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent)
             and dependent_tp_other_members_are_part_of_different_tax_family))
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /hasPtcQualifyingPlanAndQsehra
  rule ko_has_ptc_qualifying_plan_and_qsehra under condition
    has_ptc_qualifying_plan and has_qsehra
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /isAdditionalPersonInEnrollmentFamily (asked with a qualifying plan,
  # not of a dependent taxpayer)
  rule is_additional_person_in_enrollment_family under condition
    has_ptc_qualifying_plan
    and (not not_mfj_and_primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits)
    and writable_is_additional_person_in_enrollment_family
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /isAdditionalPersonPartofDifferentTaxFamily
  rule is_additional_person_partof_different_tax_family under condition
    is_additional_person_in_enrollment_family
    and writable_is_additional_person_partof_different_tax_family
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /isEnrolledWithOtherFamily (asked when the previous answer is no)
  rule is_enrolled_with_other_family under condition
    (not is_additional_person_partof_different_tax_family)
    and writable_is_enrolled_with_other_family
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /needsAllocations
  rule ko_needs_allocations under condition
    has_ptc_qualifying_plan
    and (is_additional_person_partof_different_tax_family
         or is_enrolled_with_other_family)
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /hasEmployerSponsoredPlan
  rule ko_has_employer_sponsored_plan under condition
    maybe_eligible_for_ptc and has_ptc_qualifying_plan
    and writable_has_employer_sponsored_plan
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /dependentsRequiredToFile
  rule ko_dependents_required_to_file under condition
    has_ptc_qualifying_plan and claimed_dependents_count >= 1
    and writable_dependents_required_to_file
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /selfReportedHasMultiple1095As
  rule ko_self_reported_has_multiple1095_as under condition
    has_ptc_qualifying_plan and writable_self_reported_has_multiple1095_as
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /mayPotentiallyHaveTaxFamilyWithNonEligibleImmigrationStatus
  rule may_potentially_have_tax_family_with_non_eligible_immigration_status under condition
    (is_additional_person_in_enrollment_family and not is_enrolled_with_other_family)
    or (not all_eligible_filers_are_us_citizens_or_nationals)
    or claimed_dependents_count >= 1
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /hasImmigrationStatusNotEligibleForMarketplace
  rule ko_has_immigration_status_not_eligible_for_marketplace under condition
    has_ptc_qualifying_plan
    and may_potentially_have_tax_family_with_non_eligible_immigration_status
    and writable_has_immigration_status_not_eligible_for_marketplace
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /wantsToUseAltCalculations, asked when
  # /potentiallyEligibleForAltCalcBecauseMarriedThisYear: APTC, excess APTC
  # (/netPtcAmountWhenNegative complete), married, filing jointly.
  rule ko_wants_to_use_alt_calculations under condition
    has_advanced_ptc and net_ptc_amount < $0 and is_married
    and filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
    and writable_wants_to_use_alt_calculations
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /tpNeedsToAdd1095A (with /1095AsIsDone, true for complete inputs)
  rule ko_tp_needs_to_add1095_a under condition
    has_ptc_qualifying_plan and applicable_tax_payer_or_has_aptc
    and number of form1095_as = 0
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /tpNeedsToDelete1095A ("we don't support more than 1")
  rule ko_tp_needs_to_delete1095_a under condition
    has_ptc_qualifying_plan and applicable_tax_payer_or_has_aptc
    and number of form1095_as >= 2
  consequence fulfilled

  rule unsupported under condition
    ko_dependent_tp_requires_allocations
    or ko_has_ptc_qualifying_plan_and_qsehra
    or ko_needs_allocations
    or ko_has_employer_sponsored_plan
    or ko_dependents_required_to_file
    or ko_self_reported_has_multiple1095_as
    or ko_has_immigration_status_not_eligible_for_marketplace
    or ko_wants_to_use_alt_calculations
    or ko_tp_needs_to_add1095_a
    or ko_tp_needs_to_delete1095_a
  consequence fulfilled
```
